      <h2>8. Safety and Etiquette in Talk Rooms</h2>

      <p>Group communication requires more than technical reliability. Participants also need clear expectations about privacy, behavior and moderation.</p>

      <h3>8.1 Do Not Share Sensitive Information</h3>

      <p>Avoid sharing passwords, OTPs, financial information, government identification numbers, home addresses or other sensitive information with strangers.</p>

      <h3>8.2 Respect Other Participants</h3>

      <p>Do not interrupt repeatedly, harass participants or intentionally disrupt a discussion.</p>

      <h3>8.3 Use the Microphone Responsibly</h3>

      <p>Mute your microphone when you are not speaking if background noise is interfering with the discussion.</p>

      <h3>8.4 Report Serious Problems</h3>

      <p>If a platform provides reporting tools, use them when another participant violates the community rules or behaves inappropriately.</p>

      <h3>8.5 Remember That Rooms Are Not Automatically Private</h3>

      <p>Joining a room with a limited number of participants does not mean everything said or shown should be treated as confidential. Avoid discussing information that you would not want strangers to know.</p>

